# Test: maybe-map on Some value
#
# Previously broken (B-335): The test used `[fn [x] ...]` (old-style params
# without [let]), which the runtime interprets as an extra argument — causing
# a spurious "expected 2 arguments, got 3" arity mismatch on maybe-map.
#
# Additionally, the maybe-map body had `[Some a: [f a]]` (named-arg syntax)
# instead of `[Some [f a]]` (positional). Both bugs are fixed in S-855.
#
# Remaining known issue: FunctorMaybe.fmap dispatch via the Functor typeclass
# instance is unavailable because class/instance declarations do not yet export
# instance dicts into the prelude stdlib env. Direct calls to maybe-map work.
# MonadMaybe is also not seeded in the type env (separate issue from the arity bug).
[maybe-map [fn [let x] [+ x 1]] [Some 42]]

=== out
Variant(Maybe.Some, Int(43))
